is past 12 or  13 years  I've been in this chamber for 15 years  and I have seen when austerity came in  that the first Cuts came to those things  that supported children and those things  that supported young people whether it  be our sure starts whether it be our  youth services whether it be any other  Outreach programs that we have  um it's it's incredibly unfair and that  group of people who have grown up in a  very different world to the one that I  it was privileged has has known and on  top of that we had the pandemic where  for two years children were lacking in  terms of their access to full schooling  they couldn't socialize with their  friends on a on a normal basis if you  think back to when say you were 14 two  years out of a 14 year old life is huge  and we need to do everything we can and  it's my personal mission to make sure  that children and young people are a key  Focus for this Administration this  Council it's the least we can do after  the sacrifices that they have made to  keep us all safe in the last few years  so that is one thing that I'd like to to  drive forward  another thing echoing the um probably  the spirits of of councilor Jane bore  and I'm sure and I hope she will be  approving of of this is the the very  rich cultural and sports Heritage we  have in this Borough we have a very rich  and vibrant hintle and of um of Arts  culture Leisure Sport and Heritage in  Trafford and I know there is a lot more  that we can do to drive that forward and  really put Trafford on the map where it  deserves to be we've got a culture  strategy coming up imminently and we'll  be using that to underpin everything  that we do as a council and get arts and  culture and sports and access to those  um key things  to the people of of Trafford  in previous labor councils under Dave  Acton we managed to get the Imperial War  Museum and we managed to get the  Waterside Arts Center so where we have  ambition we know that we can achieve and  we will achieve and I look forward to  working with many of you around the uh  around the chamber to do that  another key thing for me which again I  can reference two of my predecessors  Andrew Weston and Barry Brotherton is  the creation of social housing I know  back in the the 80s when Barry was  leading this organization  um he um he was instrumental in driving  more social housing at that time we have  just got our first social housing in in  recent years under Andrew Weston we need  to do a lot more on that that is has  been a priority of us for a while and it  is something that I definitely want us  to focus on going forward I also want us  to look at The Chronic housing shortage  that we have in general and the waiting  lists we have of people families  individuals looking for adequate housing  in this Borough it's not going to change  overnight and I do know the scale of the  problems that we face in terms of the  housing crisis but we need to have a  renewed focus on that area to make sure  that everyone in Trafford manages to  access a decent home  moving on to the pressing Global issues  of our time and I just want to reflect  on the um the carbon neutral action plan  which I hope colleagues in the green  party understand it is a priority of  ours it remains a priority of ours we  know that it needs to underpin  everything that we do as a council we  will be going to be called we are going  to be Governor neutral by 2038 it is  going to be a key focus of this  Administration and we obviously look  forward to working with you in terms of  in terms of achieving that but what I  also want to focus on as well is the  sheer diversity of businesses and  industries that we have in Trafford  which means that we have the potential  to lead the national debate on the green  agenda Carrington for instance is will  soon be home of Trafford green energy  which the Pioneer in production of green  of green hydrogen fuel and we're already  working with Partners in Trafford Park  to make it into a Greener more  sustainable low carbon hood for industry  again we have the opportunity to be a  flagship for driving the green agenda  and that is something that I want us to  do  one of the other things I want to to  focus on is something that I'm simply  calling getting the basics right  everything we do as a council matters  including things like gritting roads  fixing road signs maintaining grass  verges  they matter and they must be done well  and to that end our contractors need to  recognize the importance that we place  as counselors and our residence place as  local residents on getting things right  first time and we will continue to hold  our contractors to account to make sure  that residents get the best possible  service from from from that organization  other challenges that we have are  integrating our Health and Social care  to improve our outcomes and reduce  Health inequalities that is something  that we've long Believe in and it's  something that we will Long Carry On um  working on  I look forward to Leading this Council  and making it to Trafford a best a good  place for everyone to live  I really want us to continue to drive  drive the down the Gap in inequalities I  want us to recognize what a diverse and  changing Borough we have how fortunate  we all are to live in such a Borough and  celebrate it more and I'd just like to  thank each and every one of you this  evening for the very kind comments that  have come my way across each party I  know that as I have said this before and  other people have said this as well  there is more that unites us than  divides us and that has always been  something that I've held close to my  heart and that is the way that I will  approach running this Council so thank  you so much everyone  it's the real privilege and a huge honor  to take on this role it has been very  humbling listening to all the lovely  comments this evening  I never thought I'd be in this position  certainly looking back to 25 years ago I  certainly didn't think I'd be in this  position let alone being uh being the  mayor of Trafford as well but I have to  say it just brings me joy each and every  day and I will work incredibly hard for  everyone in this Borough as we look  forward to the future so thank you  thank you leader councilor Ross and as  the neutral in the chamber may I offer  my personal congratulations to you that  then is the end of the meeting I thank  everyone for your attendance hope you  enjoy the rest of your evening if anyone  wishes to join me in the mayor's parlor  for refreshment you are very welcome  thank you once again please keep safe  good night

